elated work areas? (structured prediction for IE, ontology learning, schema-guided generation, other constrained decoding methods like PICARD/Synchromesh, KG completion with type constraints, error analysis in IE)\n   - Is the positioning against existing work fair and accurate?\n\n4. **Writing Quality**\n   - Clarity of exposition\n   - Organization and flow\n   - Are negative results presented honestly?\n   - Title/abstract alignment with actual contributions\n\n5. **Weaknesses** (numbered, specific)\n\n6. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n\n7. **Minor Issues**\n\n8. **Score** (1-6) with justification\n\nFormat your review as a structured reviewer report. Be rigorous but fair. Consider whether this paper, as positioned (empirical study + targeted solution), meets the bar for a top ML venue.","uuid":"18fb4bd8-1218-4b38-989e-7f4bc94539fb","session_id":"8810d8ca-95df-4cbf-a0e9-6349587d15d7"}
