{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RyEqA8ybBgGfTZ3VsfNULL","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  venue: EMNLP 2026\\\\n  track: long paper (ARR)\\\\n  template: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n  template_note: \\\\\\\"本地无 EMNLP/ACL 模板。Worker 需下载 ACL 2023 rolling review 模板（acl2023.sty）到 templates/latex/emnlp2026/，或直接用 ARR 官方 Overleaf 模板。\\\\\\\"\\\\n  page_limit: 8  # + unlimited references + appendix\\\\n  deadline: 2026-05-25\\\\n  core_claim: >\\\\n    LLM-based IE 系统存在系统性 ontology constraint violations（15-19% per-triple），\\\\n    prompt-level 干预统计有效但 per-relation 不可靠（甚至恶化），OntoCoDec 通过\\\\n    grammar+semantic 双层 compiled constrained decoding 实现 94% DR reduction 且 F1-neutral。\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"OntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\\\\\\\"\\\\n  created_at: 2026-05-14T12:00:00Z\\\\n  approved_at: 2026-05-14\\\\n  director_adjustments:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"tab2+tab3 合并为一张 cross-dataset prompt comparison 表\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"tab4_s1_vs_s2 + fig3_ablation_layers 移至 Appendix\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"§5.3 S1 vs S2 在 main text 仅 1-2 句提及，详见 Appendix\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"Main text: tab1 + tab2_merged + tab5 + tab6 = 4 tables; fig1 + fig2 = 2 figures\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\npaper_outline:\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    word_budget: 250\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"问题：LLM-based IE 系统在 zero-shot 设置下系统性违反 ontology type constraints（SciERC 15.4%, DocRED 18.7% per-triple DR violation）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Prompt 不够：Schema-informed prompting 降低 62% violation 但 per-relation 不可靠，Evaluate-for 反而恶化 +5.8pp\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"方法：OntoCoDec 自动编译 IE ontology 为两层约束——grammar（JSON+vocabulary via XGrammar）+ semantic（cross-field domain/range via stateful entity registry + logit masking），bitwise AND 组合\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"结果：SciERC DR 15.37%→0.93%（↓94%），ET/RV→0%，F1-neutral（+0.13pp）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Limitation flag：CF violation 9.9% 作为 per-relation independent enforcement 的固有 trade-off\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    registry_refs: [phase2_scierc_unconstrained, phase2_scierc_full_s1, mvp_phase0_scierc_schema]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    word_budget: 1200\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hook: LLM 在 SciERC 上 42% 的 Compare 关系三元组违反 domain/range 约束——即使模型能正确提取实体和关系名，生成的三元组在 ontology 中是非法的\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap: 现有 constrained decoding for IE 止步于 syntactic/vocabulary 层（GCD, AdaKGC, XGrammar）；semantic type constraints（domain/range）仅 post-hoc 验证（ODKE+, OntoLogX）或限于代码生成（PLDI'25, MGD）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Insight: IE ontology constraints 有 decidability hierarchy——entity type ∈ vocab 是 purely local（grammar 可解），relation argument types 兼容 domain/range 是 prefix-decidable with state（需 entity registry），forward coreference 是 truly non-local（超出 forward-only decoding 范围）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Mechanism: OntoCoDec 自动编译 ontology schema 为两层 token-level constraints，grammar 层确保结构有效性从而 enable semantic 层做 domain/range enforcement\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Contributions: [C1] 首个系统性 violation landscape 研究——violation rate 由 constraint tightness 驱动而非 ontology size；[C2] OntoCoDec compiled constrained decoding framework with decidability taxonomy；[C3] 94% DR reduction at zero F1 cost 的实证验证\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SciERC dataset: Luan et al. 2018\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"DocRED dataset: Yao et al. 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"XGrammar: cite framework\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"GCD for IE: Geng et al. EMNLP 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"PLDI'25 type-constrained code gen\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"ODKE+ Apple 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: [fig1_overview]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    registry_refs: [mvp_phase0_violation_rate, phase2_scierc_full_s1]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: background\\\\n    word_budget: 600\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"IE ontology structure：entity types E, relation types R, domain/range mapping σ: R→P(E×E)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Grammar-constrained decoding：CFG/JSON Schema → token mask → autoregressive enforcement（XGrammar）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem statement：给定 ontology O=(E,R,σ) 和 LLM M，编译 O 为 decoding-time constraints 使输出满足 type validity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"XGrammar framework\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Outlines/SGLang for grammar decoding context\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: violation_landscape\\\\n    word_budget: 1200\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.1 实验设置：SciERC（7 relations, avg 26.1 valid pairs）+ DocRED（96 relations, avg 5.68 valid pairs），Qwen3-8B zero-shot，4 类 violation metrics（DR/RV/ET/CF）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.2 Violation 分布：SciERC DR=15.37%，DocRED DR=18.70%——comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference → violation 由 constraint tightness 驱动\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.3 Per-relation analysis：Compare 42.4%, Feature-of 33.5% vs Used-for 0.76% vs Conjunction 0%——tight constraints（few valid type pairs）→ high violation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.4 Prompt insufficiency：Schema-informed prompting SciERC ↓62.4% 但 DocRED 仅 ↓31.3%；per-relation：Evaluate-for 反而恶化 +5.8pp（prior-constraint conflict）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Standalone contribution：即使不用 OntoCoDec，violation landscape 本身是对 LLM IE 可靠性的系统性分析\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SciERC: Luan et al. 2018\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"DocRED: Yao et al. 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Qwen3: cite model\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: [fig2_per_relation_dr]\\\\n    tables: [tab2_prompt_cross_dataset]  # merged tab2+tab3\\\\n    registry_refs: [mvp_phase0_violation_rate, mvp_phase0_scierc_schema, mvp_phase0_violation_rate_docred, mvp_phase0_docred_schema]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: method\\\\n    word_budget: 1500\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.1 Decidability taxonomy：(a) purely local（entity/relation type ∈ vocab）→ grammar layer；(b) prefix-decidable with state（domain/range compatibility）→ semantic layer；(c) truly non-local（forward coreference）→ out of scope\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.2 Grammar layer：Ontology O → JSON Schema（enum entity_types, enum relation_types, array structure）→ XGrammar CFG → per-token mask M_g\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.3 Semantic layer（TypeConstraintProcessor）：stateful entity registry tracking (entity_name → entity_type) as entities are generated；relation field → lookup valid domain/range pairs → dynamic logit mask M_s\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.4 Composition：M_final = M_g ∧ M_s（bitwise AND）。Grammar 是 semantic 的 enabling prerequisite：无 grammar 保证，semantic 层遇 unknown relation type 无法查 domain/range rules\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.4 内附 Grammar-First Invariant（1-2 句设计原则，不升级为独立 claim）：'We enforce a grammar-first invariant: the semantic mask is applied only when it preserves at least one grammar-valid token, falling back to grammar-only otherwise.' 强化 enabling dependency 论点——grammar 既是 vocabulary prerequisite 也是 safety net。\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.5 S1 single-pass strategy（主推）。S2 two-pass variant 见 Appendix\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"XGrammar for grammar compilation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Synchromesh NeurIPS'22 for CSD concept\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"PLDI'25 for prefix automata analogy\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: [fig1_overview]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n    notation_table:\\\\n      O: \\\\\\\"ontology (E, R, σ)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      E: \\\\\\\"set of entity types\\\\\\\"\\\\n      R: \\\\\\\"set of relation types\\\\\\\"\\\\n      σ: \\\\\\\"domain/range mapping R → P(E×E)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      M_g: \\\\\\\"grammar layer token mask\\\\\\\"\\\\n      M_s: \\\\\\\"semantic layer token mask\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experiments\\\\n    word_budget: 2000\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.1 Setup：SciERC test（551 sentences），DocRED dev（998 docs），Qwen3-8B，4 decoding modes（unconstrained/grammar/semantic/full_s1），metrics（DR/RV/ET/CF/R-F1/E-F1）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.2 Main results（tab1）：Full S1 DR↓94%（15.37→0.93），ET/RV→0%，R-F1 +0.13pp（F1-neutral）。Grammar alone 消除 ET/RV 但不影响 DR；Semantic alone ↓24% DR 但无法消除 ET/RV → grammar 是 semantic 的前置条件\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.3 S1 vs S2：1-2 句提及 'We also evaluate a two-pass variant (S2); results comparable to S1, details in Appendix A'\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.4 Cross-dataset（DocRED, tab6）：Phase 0 prompt comparison + Phase 2 constrained results [TODO if available]\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.3 CF Analysis（tab5，双位置之一：finding）：CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入（grammar CF=0.08%=unconstrained，干净消融证据）。根因是 EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）>90%，top 冲突 Generic↔OtherScientificTerm——揭示 type system 语义边界模糊性，per-relation independent enforcement 暴露 ontology 中隐藏歧义。⚠️ 禁止 framing 为 'CF is inherent type ambiguity therefore acceptable'——正确 framing：'CF analysis reveals non-obvious type ambiguity patterns (finding), but 9.9% CF remains an open challenge for practical deployment (limitation)'\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.x Limitation paragraph：CF=9.9% 明确列为 open problem；single model（Qwen3-8B）；zero-shot only；residual DR on Evaluate-for（5.76%）\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SciERC: Luan et al. 2018\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"DocRED: Yao et al. 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: [fig2_per_relation_dr]  # fig3 moved to appendix\\\\n    tables: [tab1_main_results, tab5_cf_analysis, tab6_docred_constrained]  # tab4 moved to appendix\\\\n    registry_refs:\\\\n      - phase2_scierc_unconstrained\\\\n      - phase2_scierc_grammar_only\\\\n      - phase2_scierc_semantic_only\\\\n      - phase2_scierc_full_s1\\\\n      - phase2_scierc_full_s2\\\\n      - mvp_phase0_violation_rate_docred\\\\n      - mvp_phase0_docred_schema\\\\n      - phase2_docred_grammar_only  # [TODO: RUNNING]\\\\n      - phase2_docred_full_s1  # [TODO: RUNNING]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    word_budget: 800\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 1 — Constrained decoding for IE：GCD (EMNLP'23), AdaKGC (EMNLP'23), GoLLIE (ICLR'24) 止步 syntactic/vocabulary 层，不做 cross-field semantic constraints → OntoCoDec 补充 semantic 层\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 2 — Semantic constrained decoding (code gen)：Synchromesh (NeurIPS'22), MGD (NeurIPS'23), PLDI'25 在代码生成中做 type checking → OntoCoDec 将同一思路迁移到 IE ontology\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 3 — Ontology-guided IE：ODKE+ (Apple'25), OntoLogX ('25), SPIRES ('24) 用 ontology 指导 IE 但 post-hoc enforcement → OntoCoDec 在 decode-time prevent violations\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 4 — Type constraint enforcement (pre-LLM)：Roth & Yih (AAAI'04) ILP, KnowCoder (ACL'24) hierarchy → OntoCoDec 在 autoregressive decoding 中实现类似保证\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 5 — Constrained decoding risks：CRANE (ICML'25), Grammar-Aligned (NeurIPS'24), Hidden Cost (RANLP'25) → OntoCoDec 的 F1-neutral 结果回应此顾虑\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [introduction]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"见 literature_map.yaml must_cite 列表\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: conclusion\\\\n    word_budget: 400\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Summary：OntoCoDec 通过 compiled ontology constraints 实现 near-complete type-valid IE（DR↓94%，F1-neutral）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Key insight：violation rate 由 constraint tightness 驱动，grammar 层是 semantic 层的 enabling prerequisite\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Limitations（双位置之二：open problem）：CF=9.9% 作为 open challenge 明确列出——per-relation independent enforcement 的系统性副作用，practical deployment 需解决。Single model（Qwen3-8B）；zero-shot only。⚠️ 不能只有 §5 finding 没有 §7 limitation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Future work：global entity-type consensus during decoding（解决 CF）；cross-model validation；fine-tuned model integration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: appendix\\\\n    word_budget: 1500\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Appendix A — S1 vs S2 decoding strategies：tab4_s1_vs_s2 + fig3_ablation_layers + detailed analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Appendix B — Per-relation detailed breakdowns（all 7 SciERC relations across all modes）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Appendix C — Prompt templates（minimal vs schema-informed）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Appendix D — DocRED ontology statistics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    tables: [tab4_s1_vs_s2]\\\\n    figures: [fig3_ablation_layers]\\\\n    registry_refs: [phase2_scierc_full_s1, phase2_scierc_full_s2]\\\\n\\\\nvisualization_plan:\\\\n  # Main text figures\\\\n  - fig_id: fig1_overview\\\\n    type: conceptual\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      OntoCoDec 架构总览图。左侧：Ontology Schema（entity types, relation types, domain/range rules）。\\\\n      中间：Compiler 将 schema 编译为两层约束——上层 Grammar Layer（JSON Schema → XGrammar CFG → M_g），\\\\n      下层 Semantic Layer（domain/range rules → TypeConstraintProcessor with entity registry → M_s）。\\\\n      右侧：LLM decoding 过程，每步 logits 经 M_g ∧ M_s masking 后 sampling。\\\\n      底部注明 S1（single-pass）为主策略。\\\\n    placement: introduction\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"16:9\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig2_per_relation_dr\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      Grouped bar chart：7 个 SciERC relation types（x 轴），每个有 4 个 bar\\\\n      （unconstrained / grammar_only / semantic_only / full_s1），\\\\n      y 轴为 DR violation rate (%)。展示 full_s1 在所有 relation 上 near-zero，\\\\n      而 unconstrained 在 tight-constraint relations 上高 violation。\\\\n      辅助线标 5% threshold。按 unconstrained violation rate 降序排列 relations。\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"3:1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: phase2_scierc_unconstrained, phase2_scierc_grammar_only, phase2_scierc_semantic_only, phase2_scierc_full_s1\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  # Appendix figures\\\\n  - fig_id: fig3_ablation_layers\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      Heatmap：4 种 violation types（DR/RV/ET/CF）× 4 decoding modes\\\\n      （unconstrained/grammar/semantic/full_s1），展示每层约束消除哪些\\\\n      violation types。突出 grammar 消除 RV+ET、semantic+grammar 消除 DR、CF 作为 trade-off。\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: phase2_scierc_unconstrained, phase2_scierc_grammar_only, phase2_scierc_semantic_only, phase2_scierc_full_s1\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\ntable_plan:\\\\n  # Main text tables (4 tables)\\\\n  - table_id: tab1_main_results\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"SciERC constrained decoding results. DR/RV/ET/CF are per-triple violation rates (↓). R-F1/E-F1 are extraction F1 scores.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Mode, DR(%), RV(%), ET(%), CF(%), R-F1, E-F1]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: phase2_scierc_unconstrained, phase2_scierc_grammar_only, phase2_scierc_semantic_only, phase2_scierc_full_s1, phase2_scierc_full_s2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"加粗 full_s1 行。S2 行可保留以做 inline comparison。\\\\\\\"\\\\n    baseline_row: \\\\\\\"unconstrained\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab2_prompt_cross_dataset\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Cross-dataset prompt-level intervention. Schema-informed prompting reduces violations but scales poorly with ontology complexity.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: violation_landscape\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Dataset, \\\\\\\"|R|\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Avg Valid Pairs\\\\\\\", Prompt, DR(%), RV(%), ET(%), \\\\\\\"DR Reduction\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: mvp_phase0_violation_rate, mvp_phase0_scierc_schema, mvp_phase0_violation_rate_docred, mvp_phase0_docred_schema\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"合并原 tab2+tab3。突出 SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓31%。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab5_cf_analysis\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Cross-field consistency violation analysis. CF is 100% introduced by the semantic layer.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [Mode, \\\\\\\"CF(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"EVR entities\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"EVR rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Top conflict pattern\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: phase2_scierc_unconstrained, phase2_scierc_grammar_only, phase2_scierc_full_s1, phase2_scierc_full_s2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"数据部分来自 CF 根因分析脚本输出\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab6_docred_constrained\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Cross-dataset validation: Constrained decoding results on DocRED (96 relation types).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Mode, DR(%), RV(%), ET(%), R-F1]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: mvp_phase0_violation_rate_docred, phase2_docred_grammar_only, phase2_docred_full_s1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"[TODO] DocRED Phase 2 实验运行中，数据到后 Patch 填入\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  # Appendix tables\\\\n  - table_id: tab4_s1_vs_s2\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"S1 (single-pass) vs S2 (two-pass) decoding strategies on SciERC.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    type: ablation\\\\n    columns: [Strategy, DR(%), CF(%), R-F1, E-F1, Triples]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: phase2_scierc_full_s1, phase2_scierc_full_s2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    baseline_row: \\\\\\\"S1 (recommended)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"S2 无优势，定位为 architectural variant。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nliterature_strategy:\\\\n  citation_budget: 35\\\\n  macro_context:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"constrained decoding for structured generation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"ontology-guided information extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"type constraint enforcement in NLP/IE\\\\\\\"\\\\n  micro_clusters:\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"constrained_decoding_for_ie\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"constrained decoding information extraction 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"grammar-constrained generation NER relation extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Geng et al. EMNLP 2023 (GCD)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"AdaKGC EMNLP 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"GoLLIE ICLR 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"semantic_constrained_decoding\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"semantic constrained decoding type checking 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"type-constrained code generation LLM\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Synchromesh NeurIPS 2022\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"MGD NeurIPS 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"PLDI 2025 type-constrained code gen\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"CRANE ICML 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Grammar-Aligned Decoding NeurIPS 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"ontology_guided_ie\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"ontology-guided LLM knowledge extraction 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"schema-guided information extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"ODKE+ Apple 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SPIRES/OntoGPT Bioinformatics 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"OntoLogX 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"KnowCoder ACL 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"type_constraint_enforcement\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"type constraint entity relation extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"domain range constraint knowledge graph\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Roth & Yih 2004\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 3\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"constrained_decoding_frameworks\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"XGrammar grammar-guided generation\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"structured output LLM framework\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"XGrammar 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 2\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"constrained_decoding_risks\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"constrained decoding quality degradation 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"structured output hidden cost\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Hidden Cost RANLP 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 3\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"datasets_and_baselines\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries: []\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SciERC Luan et al. 2018\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"DocRED Yao et al. 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"EKAW 2024 ontology-constrained beam\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  - experiments\\\\n  - method\\\\n  - violation_landscape\\\\n  - introduction\\\\n  - related_work\\\\n  - abstract\\\\n  - conclusion\\\\n  - appendix\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 17380, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01E5qdXDrgD7MQ7cvXgf66Ae","session_id":"8810d8ca-95df-4cbf-a0e9-6349587d15d7","uuid":"30d0a20e-c72a-486c-a587-c94938e2bb86","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:59:44.622Z"}
